From 688e0c65d22fe216f29e63f6462a2a271429b75b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 01:10:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09290/11362] Add the retrieval half of the induction tools, so
 prefill can stop carrying every transition

The four existing tools all VERIFY a candidate against evidence the prompt already
contained; none let the prompt stop containing it. So 'we have tools now' has not
reduced context by a byte -- the tool loop calls the same induce_prompt with the same
transition count, and a multi-turn loop accumulates context rather than shrinking it.

list_transitions is the missing half: an index with NO grids -- index, action, shape,
changed-cell count, change bbox. CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_LEAN_PROMPT=N renders only N
exemplars and tells the model the rest must be fetched, so it cannot mistake a sample
for the evidence.

CONCURRENCY LEVER, NOT A CONTEXT-BUDGET ONE. Per-slot context is 153,600 tokens: a 22k
prompt and max_tokens 131072. Generation is 85%, so shrinking the prompt to zero saves
~14% and the thinking cap remains the parallelism lever. This buys PREFILL, which is
what the K=4 probe timed out on at 17k prompt tokens with 25 threads sharing 4 slots.

Bounded to session.visible, the invariant query_region already holds: an index over all
transitions would reveal the held-out tail's shape and defeat the aggregate-only split
that exposes memorisation. Returns no grids, or it rebuilds the prompt it replaces. A
reshaping transition reports -1 rather than raising.

DEFAULT OFF and byte-identical when unset; effect on quality is unmeasured and must be
A/B'd. Zero floors to 1 rather than producing an exemplar-free prompt.

9 new tests including the no-leak and no-grids invariants.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
